Revision history of WwW-GenLib


0.02_00  2026-11-01  RC
    *** REMOVE locator and location.  The former is a useless
        wrapper that offers no abstraction, and the latter is
        a fundamental conflation of file path with HAVE decla-
        rations.  Also [% O.location %] is still [% location %];
        we don't want to shadow any real configured location.

0.01_00  2026-10-31  RC
    *** read_make write_make update_file load_state read_deps
        MOVED to WwW-GenGenLib.  Please install separately.


0.00_00  2026-10-31  RC
    !>! written with substantial help from Anthropic Claude !<!

    first release!  (there is one fewer ``Gen'' since this
    isn't as general as I thought it would be (limited range
    of file names, and only one-to-one same-file-name build
    rules), but also i looked it up and learned that there's
    this thing called GNU gengen, where both Gen's stand for
    generator.)

    * locate and relapath: URL arithmetic for static sites.
      locator makes `locate' for a page; it does nothing to
      the spec but locate (no index.html rewrite; that is
      for each site to decide).

      locate was ported from www-cellar, which was in turn
      ported from the cooper-www experiment.  Many helps to
      Claude for the edge case handling prior to porting.

    * location: where in the site a page is; accessible in
      render via [% O.location %].
      (Not [% location %]!!! render can now access %D vars
        (${B}/MY/config.mk) as well because we want it to
        know where its peers live.)  [This is wrong; see 0.2]

    * read_make/write_make/update_file/load_state: MY/config.mk
      and MY/option.mk, written only if they changed (mtime
      kept, so reconfiguring does not rebuild the world).

    * read_deps: HAVE/NEED/WANT headers in any comment style,
      REM and :: included.  Paths are from the project root
      and are expanded by siteconf (see its docs).

    * parse_base: sanitize site_url and base_url.

      This is also a port, with the special handling of `/'
      base_url patched by Claude too.
